The STAR [4] detector shown in Fig. 2.6, is designed primarily for the measurement of hadrons production over a large solid angle. It is a large acceptance detector which covers the full azimuthal (\(0\leq\phi\leq 2\pi\)) for \(|\eta|<1.8\) and \(2.5<|\eta|<4.0\). It consists of second biggest working Time Projection Chamber for particle tracking. The STAR also has a number of sub-detectors, discussed in detail in the following sections.

