#### Upper Limit on \(v_{2}\) Fluctuations

In order to compare our data with models for eccentricity fluctuations we compare \(\sigma_{v_{2}}/v_{2}\) to \(\sigma_{\varepsilon}/\varepsilon\). From the two- and four-particle cumulant data however, we can't uniquely determine the value of \(\sigma_{v_{2}}\) since \(v_{2}\{2\}^{2}-v_{2}\{4\}^{2}\approx\delta_{2}+2\sigma_{v_{2}}\). However, we can derive an upper limit to the ratio \(\sigma_{v_{2}}/v_{2}\) by setting \(\delta_{2}=0\). This amounts to assuming that the difference between the second and fourth order cumulant is dominated by \(v_{2}\) fluctuations. For the Gaussian form of the fluctuations the parameters \(\langle v\rangle\), \(\sigma_{v_{2}}\) and \(\delta_{2}\) are correlated according to [25]:

\[v_{2}\{2\}^{2} = \langle v\rangle^{2}+\sigma_{v_{2}}^{2}+\delta_{2} \tag{6.12}\] \[v_{2}\{4\}^{2} = \sqrt{\langle v\rangle^{4}-2\langle v\rangle^{2}\sigma_{v_{2}}^{ 2}-\sigma_{v_{2}}^{4}}\approx\langle v\rangle^{2}-\sigma_{v_{2}}^{2} \tag{6.13}\]

Figure 6.23: Comparison of \(v_{2}\{2\}^{2}-v_{2}\{4\}^{2}\) with \(\sigma_{\varepsilon}\) for Au+Au and Cu+Cu collisions at 200 and 62.4 GeV with \(\sigma_{\varepsilon}\) from the eccentricity models (a) MCG-N (b) MCG-Q (c) fKLN-CGC.

For convenience, we define two parameters \(\Sigma\) and \(\Delta\) using the Eq. (6.12) and Eq. (6.13)

\[\Sigma = \frac{v_{2}\{2\}^{2}+v_{2}\{4\}^{2}}{2}=\frac{\delta_{2}}{2}+\langle v \rangle^{2} \tag{6.14}\] \[\Delta = \frac{v_{2}\{2\}^{2}-v_{2}\{4\}^{2}}{2}=\frac{\delta_{2}}{2}+ \sigma_{v_{2}}^{2} \tag{6.15}\]

Taking \(\delta_{2}=0\) in the above equations, the ratio

\[\sqrt{\frac{v_{2}\{2\}^{2}-v_{2}\{4\}^{2}}{v_{2}\{2\}^{2}+v_{2}\{4\}^{2}}}, \tag{6.16}\]

becomes an upper limit to the ratio \(\sigma_{v_{2}}/\langle v_{2}\rangle\) where, in the case that \(v_{2}\) fluctuations are dominated by eccentricity fluctuations, \(\langle v_{2}\rangle\) is the average \(v_{2}\) relative to the participant axis. The \(\sigma_{v}/v\) from the data has been compared with \(\sigma_{\varepsilon}/\varepsilon\) from the models. Under the assumption \(v_{2}\propto\varepsilon\), the \(\sigma_{\varepsilon}/\varepsilon\) derived from the models as:

\[\frac{\sigma_{\varepsilon}^{2}}{\varepsilon^{2}}=\frac{\varepsilon\{2\}^{2}- \varepsilon\{4\}^{2}}{\varepsilon\{2\}^{2}+\varepsilon\{4\}^{2}} \tag{6.17}\]where \(\varepsilon\{2\}^{2}=\langle\varepsilon_{part}^{2}\rangle\) and \(\varepsilon\{4\}^{4}=-\langle\varepsilon_{part}^{4}\rangle+2\langle\varepsilon_{ part}^{2}\rangle^{2}\), \(\varepsilon_{part}\) is the eccentricity calculated in the participant plane.

